<header class="hero hero-ide" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="kicker">Spec-first agentic development</p>
      <h1>Vibe coding is dead. <em>Talk it through, the rest is guided.</em></h1>
      <div class="hero-split">
        <p class="lede">Describe the feature in your own words. Four commands write the spec, check it against your code, build it in its own worktree and deliver it through your checks. Run several side by side and get back verified pull requests.</p>
        <div>
          <div class="hero-row2">
            <div class="cmd">
              <code id="cmd1"><span>/plugin marketplace add</span> holgerleichsenring/specification-first-agentic-development</code>
              <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="cmd1">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <a class="btn btn-ink" href="#install">Install</a>
          </div>
          <div class="facts"><span>MIT licensed</span><span>Plain YAML and Markdown in your repo</span><span>Claude Code plugin, or any agent</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-scene">
      <div class="ide-steps" role="group" aria-label="Steps of the example">
        <button type="button" data-step="0" aria-pressed="false"><b>1</b>Describe</button>
        <button type="button" data-step="1" aria-pressed="false"><b>2</b>/create-spec</button>
        <button type="button" data-step="2" aria-pressed="true"><b>3</b>/review-spec</button>
        <button type="button" data-step="3" aria-pressed="false"><b>4</b>/apply-spec</button>
        <button type="button" data-step="4" aria-pressed="false"><b>5</b>/deliver-spec</button>
      </div>

      <div class="ide-stage">
        <div class="bubble b0" data-show="0" hidden><b>You talk, it listens</b>You describe the app in your own words. Before asking anything, the agent reads your memory and the repository, so it only asks what neither can answer.</div>
        <div class="bubble b1" data-show="1" hidden><b>The spec comes first</b>create-spec writes goal, facts with file and line, steps and done criteria, on a fresh branch in its own worktree. No code yet.</div>
        <div class="bubble b2" data-show="2"><b>A second pair of eyes</b>A script checks that every cited file and line exists. Then a new agent with no chat history attacks the spec against the code, and its cuts are applied before anything is built.</div>
        <div class="bubble b3" data-show="3" hidden><b>Built by the spec</b>apply-spec works through the steps, writes the tests the spec names, and logs every choice that wasn't obvious in decisions/.</div>
        <div class="bubble b4" data-show="4" hidden><b>Only green lands</b>The commit goes through the gate: build and tests have to pass. Then the branch is pushed and the pull request opens with the spec inside.</div>

